        "type": "slimmer",
        "tekst": "**In plain words**\n\nAs societies get more advanced technology, inequality first goes up a lot (farming societies with lords and serfs) and then comes down a bit (industrial societies with education and rights): that's the Kuznets curve. The Bell Curve book claimed rich people are simply smarter, but critics showed that's mostly about upbringing and opportunities."
