        "type": "slimmer",
        "tekst": "**In plain words**\n\nThe world has a tiny super-rich group, a billion people in deep poverty, and the rest of us in between, still divided by class, gender, ethnicity, age and more, all mixing together ([[intersectionality|Intersectionality]]). Inequality is about what you have, how you're pushed out, and how it feels. Total forced equality, though, can be a nightmare too, as Vonnegut's story shows."
